#HELP_BEGIN
IV-CAM PTZ Presets v1.0

Expandable buttons for the presets on IV-CAM PTZ v1.0.

Press[n] recalls camera preset n. Holding it for Hold_Time stores that preset.
Press[1] is preset 1. The symbol starts with one button and expands to 32.

One preset runs at a time. A new press cancels the press already in progress.
Releasing the cancelled button does nothing.

Press_FB[n] follows Press[n]. After a store it drops for Blink_Time, then
follows the button again. That drop is the store confirmation.

Preset_Trigger recalls preset 0 through 255 when the analog changes.
The value sitting on it at startup waits for the next change.
Send a different number before sending the same number again.
A value above 255 is sent as 255.
Preset 0 is a camera memory. Home on IV-CAM PTZ is a different command.

Wire this symbol to IV-CAM PTZ v1.0:
  Store   -> Store_Preset
  Recall  -> Recall_Preset
  Preset  -> Preset

Store and Recall pulse on each recall or store. Preset changes to the
preset number before that pulse.

Hold_Time default is 3s, range 0.5s to 10s.
Blink_Time default is 0.5s, range 0s to 5s. At 0s, Press_FB stays with
the button through the store.

Rows:
  1  Hold_Time
  2  Blink_Time
  3  Store
  4  Recall
  5  blank
  6+ Press[n] beside Press_FB[n]
  blank
  Preset_Trigger beside Preset
  Adding a button moves the blank row and Preset_Trigger down.
  Hold_Time, Blink_Time, Store, and Recall stay on the first rows.

v1.0  2026-11-06
- Press recalls, hold stores, feedback drops to confirm a store
- One wait. A new press cancels the press already in progress
- Preset_Trigger recalls by number
#HELP_END

#HINT "Press recalls an IV-CAM preset. Hold stores it."
#CATEGORY "19" // Camera
#DEFAULT_VOLATILE
#ENABLE_DYNAMIC
#ENABLE_STACK_CHECKING
#DIGITAL_EXPAND InputsWithOutputs

#DEFINE_CONSTANT MaxPresets 32
#DEFINE_CONSTANT PhaseHold 1
#DEFINE_CONSTANT PhaseBlink 2

/*
	Row 1   Hold_Time
	Row 2   Blink_Time
	Row 3                             Store
	Row 4                             Recall
	Row 5   blank
	Rows 6+ Press[n]                  Press_FB[n]
	blank
	        Preset_Trigger            Preset
	One wait, PressWait. A new press cancels it and owns the timer.
	Release during the hold cancels it and recalls. When it expires,
	the preset is stored and the same wait drops feedback for Blink_Time.
	Hold_Time and Blink_Time are hundredths, the same unit as Wait.
*/

DIGITAL_INPUT	_SKIP_, _SKIP_, _SKIP_, _SKIP_, _SKIP_, Press[MaxPresets,1];
DIGITAL_OUTPUT	_SKIP_, _SKIP_, Store, Recall, _SKIP_, Press_FB[MaxPresets,1];

ANALOG_INPUT	_SKIP_, Preset_Trigger;
ANALOG_OUTPUT	_SKIP_, Preset;

INTEGER_PARAMETER	Hold_Time, Blink_Time;

#BEGIN_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES Hold_Time
	propValidUnits =		unitTime;
	propDefaultUnit =		unitTime;
	propBounds =			0.5s, 10.0s;
	propDefaultValue =		3.0s;
	propShortDescription =	"Hold this long to store";
	#BEGIN_PROP_FULL_DESCRIPTION
		How long Press[n] stays high before that preset is stored.
		A release before this recalls the preset.
	#END_PROP_FULL_DESCRIPTION
#END_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES

#BEGIN_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES Blink_Time
	propValidUnits =		unitTime;
	propDefaultUnit =		unitTime;
	propBounds =			0.0s, 5.0s;
	propDefaultValue =		0.5s;
	propShortDescription =	"How long feedback drops after a store";
	#BEGIN_PROP_FULL_DESCRIPTION
		After a store, Press_FB[n] stays low for this long, then follows
		the button again. 0s keeps the feedback on the button.
	#END_PROP_FULL_DESCRIPTION
#END_PARAMETER_PROPERTIES

INTEGER Ready, Active, Waiting, NextSpan, Down[MaxPresets];

FUNCTION ShowFb (INTEGER i) {
	INTEGER level;

	If (IsSignalDefined(Press_FB[i]) = 0)
		Return;
	If (Waiting = PhaseBlink) {
		If (Active = i)
			level = 0;
		Else If (Down[i] = 1)
			level = 1;
		Else
			level = 0;
	}
	Else If (Down[i] = 1)
		level = 1;
	Else
		level = 0;
	If (Press_FB[i] <> level)
		Press_FB[i] = level;
}

FUNCTION PulseCamera (INTEGER storing) {
	INTEGER fell;

	fell = 0;
	If (Store <> 0) {
		Store = 0;
		fell = 1;
	}
	If (Recall <> 0) {
		Recall = 0;
		fell = 1;
	}
	If (fell = 1)
		ProcessLogic();
	If (storing = 1)
		Store = 1;
	Else
		Recall = 1;
	ProcessLogic();
	If (storing = 1)
		Store = 0;
	Else
		Recall = 0;
}

FUNCTION Drive (INTEGER n, INTEGER storing) {
	If (n > 255)
		n = 255;
	If (Preset <> n)
		Preset = n;
	PulseCamera(storing);
}

FUNCTION OnPressWait () {
	INTEGER n;

	NextSpan = 0;
	n = Active;
	If (Waiting = PhaseHold) {
		Waiting = 0;
		Active = 0;
		If (n < 1)
			Return;
		Drive(n, 1);
		If (Blink_Time = 0) {
			ShowFb(n);
			Return;
		}
		If (Waiting <> 0)
			Return;
		Active = n;
		Waiting = PhaseBlink;
		ShowFb(n);
		NextSpan = Blink_Time;
	}
	Else If (Waiting = PhaseBlink) {
		Waiting = 0;
		Active = 0;
		If (n >= 1)
			ShowFb(n);
	}
}

FUNCTION ArmPressWait (INTEGER span) {
	Wait (span, PressWait) {
		OnPressWait();
		If (NextSpan <> 0)
			ArmPressWait(NextSpan);
	}
}

FUNCTION CancelPressWait () {
	CancelWait(PressWait);
}

FUNCTION ClearActive () {
	INTEGER old;

	If (Active = 0)
		Return;
	old = Active;
	CancelPressWait();
	Active = 0;
	Waiting = 0;
	NextSpan = 0;
	ShowFb(old);
}

PUSH Press {
	INTEGER i;

	If (Ready = 0)
		Return;
	i = GetLastModifiedArrayIndex();
	If (i < 1)
		Return;
	If (i > MaxPresets)
		Return;
	If (Active <> 0)
		ClearActive();
	Down[i] = 1;
	Active = i;
	Waiting = PhaseHold;
	ShowFb(i);
	ArmPressWait(Hold_Time);
}

RELEASE Press {
	INTEGER i;

	If (Ready = 0)
		Return;
	i = GetLastModifiedArrayIndex();
	If (i < 1)
		Return;
	If (i > MaxPresets)
		Return;
	If (Down[i] = 0)
		Return;
	Down[i] = 0;
	If (Active = i) {
		If (Waiting = PhaseHold) {
			CancelPressWait();
			Active = 0;
			Waiting = 0;
			NextSpan = 0;
			Drive(i, 0);
		}
	}
	ShowFb(i);
}

CHANGE Preset_Trigger {
	INTEGER n;

	If (Ready = 0)
		Return;
	If (Waiting = PhaseHold)
		ClearActive();
	n = Preset_Trigger;
	Drive(n, 0);
}

FUNCTION Main() {
	WaitForInitializationComplete();
	Ready = 1;
}
